<h2>🎨 Step 7: Flutter UI Tree Integration Logic</h2>

<p>To render an interactive 5-level expandable tree in Flutter Widgets:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Top Levels (1–3):</strong> Use nested <code>ExpansionTile</code> widgets to display Maha, Antar, and Pratyantar Dasha items retrieved from <code>/full-report</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Expansion Event:</strong> In the <code>onExpansionChanged</code> callback of the Level 3 (Pratyantar) <code>ExpansionTile</code>, check if Sookshma sub-nodes exist in your local state.</li>
  <li><strong>On-Demand Fetching:</strong> If null, show a <code>CircularProgressIndicator</code> and trigger <code>fetchPranaDashaTree()</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>State Update:</strong> Store fetched <code>sookshma_dashas</code> in a local <code>setState()</code> or Provider/Riverpod state to dynamically display Levels 4 and 5.</li>
</ol>

